    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Let me summarize the change.\n\n## Summary\n\nI consolidated all duplicate detection into a single derived `identityKey` and made the API return it.\n\n**`identityKey` = `normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + (householdId or empty)`**. An owner is rejected with 409 only when its *whole* key equals an existing owner's. Since the telephone is part of the key, two household members with different telephones get different keys and are both allowed \u2014 only an exact full-key match is a duplicate.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`IdentityKey.java`** (new, small cohesive class) \u2014 `of(owner)` derives the key (telephone is already E.164-normalized by the existing request validator; email is already lower-cased), and `isDuplicate(candidate, existing)` does the single full-key equality check.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 replaced the three separate checks (telephone / `DuplicateEmails` / `HouseholdDuplicates.isRejectedDuplicate`) with one `IdentityKey.isDuplicate(...)` call, keeping the unrelated `CityCapacity` check. `assignHousehold` now runs *before* the check so the candidate's `householdId` is part of its key. This also lowers the method's cyclomatic complexity (the conflict condition drops from four `||` operands to two) and removes two lines.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` expression so every returned `OwnerDto` carries `identityKey` (reusing `IdentityKey.of`, no duplicated logic).\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `identityKey` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated DTO exposes it.\n\nStructural impact was kept low: the duplicate logic lives in a new tiny class rather than growing `Owner` or the large controller; the controller edit both shrinks and simplifies `addOwner`; and the dead helpers (`DuplicateEmails`, `HouseholdDuplicates.isRejectedDuplicate`) were left untouched rather than touching more files to remove them.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest` (identity-collision \u2192 409) and the full suite pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
